sequenceDiagram
autonumber
participant Admin as Administrator
participant Client as browser-cert-fetcher (local tool)
participant IdP as Identity Provider<br/>(Keycloak / Okta / etc.)
participant CertIssuer as cert-issuer
participant CA as CA (in-process, part of cert-issuer)
Admin->>Client: Run tool
activate Client
Client->>Client: Generate keypair locally<br/>(private key never leaves this machine)
Client->>Client: Build CSR (public key + requested identity)
Client->>IdP: Initiate Authorization Code flow
deactivate Client
activate IdP
IdP-->>Admin: Present login (password, smart card/PIV, MFA -- <br/>whatever this realm is configured for)
Admin->>IdP: Authenticate directly with IdP<br/>(Client never sees credentials)
IdP-->>Client: Authorization code
deactivate IdP
activate Client
Client->>IdP: Exchange code for access token
deactivate Client
activate IdP
IdP-->>Client: Access token (JWT)<br/>iss, aud, identity claim, exp
deactivate IdP

activate Client
Client->>CertIssuer: POST /issue<br/>Authorization: Bearer (token)<br/>body: { csr_pem, cert_type }
deactivate Client
activate CertIssuer
CertIssuer->>CertIssuer: Peek unverified iss claim
CertIssuer->>CertIssuer: Select matching trusted IssuerConfig<br/>(by iss -- determines which JWKS/audience/<br/>claim-path config to use)
CertIssuer->>IdP: Fetch JWKS for this issuer<br/>
activate IdP
IdP-->>CertIssuer: Signing keys
deactivate IdP
CertIssuer->>CertIssuer: Verify signature, issuer, audience, exp<br/>(all scoped to the selected issuer)
CertIssuer->>CertIssuer: Extract identity claim via this issuer's<br/>configured claim path
CertIssuer->>CertIssuer: Verify CSR's SAN matches extracted identity<br/>(same check used for workload certs today)
CertIssuer->>CA: Sign CSR
activate CA
note over CA: Not a separate service --<br/>the rcgen-backed CA that runs<br/>inside cert-issuer's own process.
CA-->>CertIssuer: Signed certificate
deactivate CA
CertIssuer-->>Client: Signed certificate
deactivate CertIssuer
activate Client
Client->>Client: Store cert alongside already-held<br/>private key (e.g. import into browser<br/>NSS store)
deactivate Client
Note over CertIssuer: Future extension point (not built today):<br/>report issuance to a Credentials Agent,<br/>which writes a provenance node to the graph<br/>-- same pattern as every other observed resource.
